-- a setting: the temperature, the order of magnitude of the rate the observation resolves, and whether
-- the medium is chiral. For proton resonance the resolving rate is the separation of the shifts in hertz,
-- which is a property of the instrument and of the pair of shifts and not of the molecule -- which is why
-- it belongs here.
Setting : Type 0
Setting = (temp : Nat) × ((res : Nat) × Bool)
